rcontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T05:47:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T05:47:04Z","body":"I'd avoid \"Optimize For:\" wording because it can lowkey sound like it will do more than settings, like it will start precompiling case-specific shaders or something like that. Just \"Project Settings:\" would be less ambiguous, makes it clear that it only changes settings. Then you can rename \"(none)\" to \"Default\".\r\n\r\nAlso the full list of settings probably shouldn't be shown in the project creation dialog, the UI is already too busy. there could be an icon button next to the dropdown to open the full presets dialog where you can see the full list, configure presets in the future, etc.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5434913716/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5454230638","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122615#issuecomment-5454230638","